<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine car output climbed nine pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Argentine car output climbed nine pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's car output in 1996 was nine percent up on 1995 at 312,072 units, state news agency Telam reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>Production for December was 24,915 vehicles, which was 37 percent higher than the same month of 1995 but down 21 percent on November last year for seasonal reasons, Telam said. It was quoting data from the car industry lobby ADEFA, which had been expected to announce the figures later Tuesday.</p>
<p>((-Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0695))</p>
